From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nomorecoolnicknames <nomorecoolnicknames@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 02:04:57 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] gd: hci: keep the pages read when a later extended-features
 page fails

Some controllers announce a maximum page of Read Local Extended Features
that they cannot read. The MediaTek CONSYS Bluetooth 4.0 core of the Meizu
M5c (MT6737M, local name "MTK MT0335", HCI version 6) answers:

  Read Local Extended Features page 0 -> success, maximum page 2
  Read Local Extended Features page 1 -> success, maximum page 2
  Read Local Extended Features page 2 -> 0x30 Parameter Out Of Mandatory Range

and Controller::impl::read_local_extended_features_complete_handler()
turned that into an abort of com.android.bluetooth on every enable:

  assertion 'status == ErrorCode::SUCCESS' failed - Status 0x30

Keep the pages already read and finish the start-up. A controller that
fails page 0 still aborts as before.

Change-Id: I2c72ddc0ab8391e58c8b3468c23acb3385a0b968

diff --git a/system/gd/hci/controller.cc b/system/gd/hci/controller.cc
index 10023e3..a4bddaf 100644
--- a/system/gd/hci/controller.cc
+++ b/system/gd/hci/controller.cc
@@ -280,6 +280,18 @@ struct Controller::impl {
     auto complete_view = ReadLocalExtendedFeaturesCompleteView::Create(view);
     ASSERT(complete_view.IsValid());
     ErrorCode status = complete_view.GetStatus();
+    // Some controllers announce a maximum page they cannot read.  The MediaTek
+    // CONSYS Bluetooth 4.0 core of the Meizu M5c ("MTK MT0335") answers pages
+    // 0 and 1 with maximum page 2, and page 2 with 0x30 (Parameter Out Of
+    // Mandatory Range).  Keep the pages already read instead of aborting the
+    // stack; a controller that cannot even give page 0 still aborts.
+    if (status != ErrorCode::SUCCESS && !extended_lmp_features_array_.empty()) {
+      LOG_WARN("Read Local Extended Features page %zu failed: %s; using the first %zu page(s)",
+               extended_lmp_features_array_.size(), ErrorCodeText(status).c_str(),
+               extended_lmp_features_array_.size());
+      promise.set_value();
+      return;
+    }
     ASSERT_LOG(status == ErrorCode::SUCCESS, "Status 0x%02hhx, %s", status, ErrorCodeText(status).c_str());
     uint8_t page_number = complete_view.GetPageNumber();
     extended_lmp_features_array_.push_back(complete_view.GetExtendedLmpFeatures());
